ImageViewer patch (docs/PLAN.md section 15, D-57, D-93): filters drawn only where they reach the visible area
Library: resvg 0.48.1
Fixes: none (speed: SVG filters cost as much as their whole region, linebender/resvg#790 and #1192)
Upstream: none yet: to be proposed to linebender/resvg, linked to #1192 (ours)
Remove when: a resvg release draws a filtered layer only within reach of the canvas and reuses equal feTurbulence results, or this patch no longer applies

resvg drew every filtered group over its whole filter region, at the scale asked, however little of
it the canvas shows: a region of the canvas cost as much as the whole document, and a zoomed-in view
of a document with filters cost its whole area at that zoom. Here:
- a layer is drawn only within reach of the visible area (render::Context::visible): for a filtered
  group, the reach of its filters (filter::reach(): the box blur's exact width, offsets, morphology,
  displacement, convolution, lighting); a filter whose result may depend on its whole region
  (feTile, feImage, stitched feTurbulence) keeps its whole region, as before. Groups outside the
  reach are not drawn at all, nor are layers outside the visible area (tiny-skia 0.12 drew a one-row
  pixmap placed just above the canvas onto the canvas's first row);
- a primitive's subregion is cleared around within its result's pixels, wherever the subregion lies
  (it may now lie partly or wholly outside a layer drawn only in part);
- equal feTurbulence results (same noise over the same pixels) are computed once per render
  (filter::Cache, the four most recent): a document may use one noise in several filters.
The pixels are those of the whole region, but for anti-aliased edges, whose coverage may differ by a
rounding step when a layer starts elsewhere (as between any two tiles): 3 of resvg's 1,730 reference
images differ there (filters/filter/content-outside-the-canvas-2, painting/marker/with-an-image-child,
structure/image/preserveAspectRatio=xMidYMid-slice-on-svg).

